WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.200
-Well, results from last
night's wild midterm elections

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.434
are still rolling in

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.501
and several races are still
too close to call,

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:10.334
including control of both
the House and Senate,

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:11.934
so, we have to be patient.

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:14.634
As of right now, our decision
desk here at "Late Night"

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:16.567
is using very cautious language

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:19.033
to describe the state
of the race this way.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:21.234
"With 87%
of precincts reporting,

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:22.100
we can now project the...

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.601
I forgot to mention
our election guy is

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:29.467
from New Jersey, like Dr. Oz.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:31.567
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:35.133
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:38.734
Oh, man!
Where to begin, you guys?

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:41.501
I turned my phone off last night
at 7:00 pm and went to bed.

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:42.667
Didn't even check the results

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.167
until I dropped my kids
off at school,

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.434
so, I am well-rested
and feeling good.

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:48.067
Now, you might say, "Seth,

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:50.167
you knew you'd have to address
the election today.

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:51.667
How could you just
tune out like that?"

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:53.901
It's easy. I made my staff
pull an all-nighter.

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:55.767
[ Laughter ]
And, it should be noted,

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.300
they look like [bleep] today.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.067
[ Laughter ]
Point is, I tuned out because,

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:02.601
as I'm sure you all heard,
going into this election,

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:04.300
pundits,
especially on the right,

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.200
but across the media spectrum,
were certain the Democrats

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.133
were going to get
absolutely annihilated.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.701
-Fifteen days to the midterms

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:13.400
and there's more and more signs
of a red wave.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.667
-I really believe
it's going to be

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:17.133
a strong red wave
for the Republicans.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.567
-It's going to be
a big red wave.

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.000
-Do you think
the red wave is coming?

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.167
I mean, like "Winter is coming,"
it's red wave coming?

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.167
-You're of the mind-set

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:25.067
it's red wave.
-Absolutely.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:27.634
-I think that this is going
to be a big red wave.

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:29.767
-It'll be a huge red wave

00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:31.667
and it'll be
a big blue wipeout.

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.501
-They are very,
very concerned about this,

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.434
you know, red riptide,
if not a red wave,

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:36.901
if not a red tsunami.

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:38.334
-I see,
not a red wave.

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.033
I see a red tsunami.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.100
-We're not just going
to see a red wave.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.634
We're going
to see a red tsunami.

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:45.567
[ Laughter ]
-Now, that last one was a bit
of a giveaway

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.767
because, if there was truly
a tsunami coming,

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.200
we all know Ted Cruz
would've been

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.767
on the first flight to Cancun.

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:51.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.067
[ As Cruz ]
Red waves are great,

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:54.567
but I prefer the blue waves

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:56.467
outside the Cancun Ritz Carlton.

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:58.467
[ Laughter ]
I'll bring you back
a conk fritter.

00:01:58.467 --> 00:01:59.767
Stay warm, everybody.

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:02.801
Also, I did appreciate
the "Game of Thrones" reference.

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:04.234
-Do you think
the red wave is coming?

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.734
I mean, like "Winter is coming,"
it's red wave coming?

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:08.033
[ Laughter ]
-I would say it was less like
a red wave

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:09.501
and more like a Red Wedding.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:10.334
[ Laughter ]
-The Republicans were the Starks

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:11.701
and Donald Trump was a dragon

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.701
who burned his whole
[bleep] party to a crisp.

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:16.267
[ Laughter ]
And don't just take
my word for it.

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:17.300
Listen to Republicans

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.801
and right-wing pundits
themselves,

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:21.501
who spent the last 24 hours
wringing their hands,

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.267
wondering where it
all went wrong.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:26.000
-I thought the political
conditions were such

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.133
that would suggest a red wave.

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:31.067
The polling said otherwise

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:33.501
and I was skeptical
of the polling.

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:35.100
The polling's held up
pretty well tonight.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.033
-The big red wave
that was predicted

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:39.367
has not happened yet.

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:41.000
-There wasn't
a red wave.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.501
[ Laughter ]
That is a searing indictment

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:43.868
of the Republican Party.

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:45.701
That is a searing indictment
of the message

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:47.467
that we have been sending
to the voters.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:51.501
The Republican Party needs to do
a really deep introspection,

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:52.667
look in the mirror right now

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:55.334
because this is
an absolute disaster.

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:57.234
-Definitely not
a Republican wave,

00:02:57.234 --> 00:02:58.400
that's for darn sure.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.267
-[ As Graham ]
This is definitely not

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:00.334
a Republican wave.

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:02.567
It was more like
the wave my Meemaw makes

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.334
when she jumps
in the bathtub with me.

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:06.167
[ Laughter ]
She barely moves the water

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.501
because she's about 84 pounds
soaking wet.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.734
Meemaw, I'm a grown man!

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:12.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:15.167
I don't take baths
with you anymore, Meemaw!

00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:16.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.200
Now, on one hand,

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.767
there's still much
to be decided.

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:20.167
Control of both houses
of Congress

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:21.534
is, essentially,
a toss-up right now

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.067
and Republicans could still
end up winning

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:25.767
both the House and the Senate,
so, it's wise to be cautious.

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:28.267
But on the other hand, despite
strong political head winds,

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:29.734
including the fact
that, historically,

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:32.300
the party in power tends
to get swamped in the midterms,

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.100
the race for both
the House and Senate

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.400
is, essentially,
a toss-up as of this taping,

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.534
which is crazy.

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:39.133
Democrats actually flipped
some long-held

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:40.934
Republican House seats
in states like Ohio,

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:42.701
while also winning back
governorships

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:44.267
in states like Maryland
and Massachusetts;

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:46.701
Americans voted
to protect abortion rights

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:48.767
in several states,
through ballot initiatives,

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.033
including in Kentucky;

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:51.868
expanded Medicaid
in South Dakota;

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:54.067
guaranteed a right to unionize
in Illinois;

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.934
and legalized marijuana
in Missouri.

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:57.467
At this point,
I wouldn't be shocked

00:03:57.467 --> 00:04:00.267
if we found out voters in Kansas
passed a ballot initiative to...

00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:04.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:06.968
Which they should, because that
would be fun as hell!

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:08.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:09.667
By far, the most dramatic,

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:12.033
and my favorite, example
of how poorly things went

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:14.167
for Republicans last night
is a shocking development

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.133
in Colorado's
3rd Congressional District,

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:18.667
where Lauren Boebert is,
as of this taping,

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:20.100
trailing her
Democratic opponent

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.234
in a race absolutely no one
thought would be competitive.

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:25.234
-In Colorado, a hardline
pro-Trump Republican

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:26.033
on the ropes.

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.434
Congresswoman Lauren Boebert

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:29.834
behind by a few thousand votes
right now.

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:31.834
-This is Lauren Boebert's
seat here.

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:33.400
Not even a seat
that we considered

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.033
to be competitive,
leading into Election Day.

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:39.467
Lauren Boebert is trailing
by about 3,500 votes.

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:41.200
Lauren Boebert is

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:46.300
an election denying,
very conservative Republican.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.467
Democrats would love
to unseat her.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.901
I'm not sure they thought
they had a chance to.

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:52.167
They have a chance.

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:53.834
-I'm not saying I was excited
last night

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:55.534
when I saw those results,
but I did rush

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:57.667
into my kids' room at 3:00 am
to shake them and scream,

00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:00.067
"Wake up!
Lauren Boebert is losing!"

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:02.133
[ Laughter ]
And they know who she is

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.501
because I tell them, if they
don't eat their vegetables,

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:05.601
they'll get a visit from...

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:08.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:10.133
By the way, if you're
confusing her with Sarah Palin,

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:12.100
who's also running for Congress
this year in Alaska,

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.400
don't worry --
they're both losing,

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.501
so you don't even need
to give them straight.

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:16.701
[ Laughter ]
By far, the biggest prize

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:17.968
of the night was
in Pennsylvania,

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:20.234
where both the governorship
and the Senate seat,

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:21.968
which is held
by a retiring Republican,

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:24.367
were seen as two of the most
closely watched races

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:25.901
when election season began.

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:28.167
Democratic candidate
for governor Josh Shapiro

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:29.734
ran away with it and crushed

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:32.767
his pro-Trump election denier
opponent, Doug Mastriano.

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:34.701
But the even bigger victory
for Democrats,

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.467
and, possibly, the biggest
disappointment in the night

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:38.601
for Republicans,
was the Senate race.

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:39.968
-Fox News can project

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:42.467
that Lieutenant Governor
John Fetterman

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:47.701
will win the Pennsylvania Senate
race over Dr. Mehmet Oz.

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:50.934
This is a huge win
for the Democrats.

00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:52.567
-Wow!
I can't believe a candidate

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:55.000
with no government experience,
who lives in New Jersey

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.334
and reportedly killed
over 300 dogs

00:05:57.334 --> 00:06:00.133
[ Laughter ]
lost a race for Senate
in Pennsylvania.

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:01.767
[ Laughter ]
The only way Oz could've been

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:03.334
a worse candidate
in Pennsylvania was

00:06:03.334 --> 00:06:05.033
if he was seen
in a Devils jersey,

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:06.334
fighting with Gritty,
screaming,

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:09.300
"7-Eleven is better
than Wawa and Sheetz."

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:12.934
Oz's closing argument included,
among other things,

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:15.300
posting an incredibly bizarre
photo of himself

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:16.467
[ Laughter ]
standing under a sign

00:06:16.467 --> 00:06:18.467
displaying gas prices
on the side of the road,

00:06:18.467 --> 00:06:21.267
like he was looking to sell some
of his off-brand diet pills

00:06:21.267 --> 00:06:23.601
and urging people,
this past Saturday,

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:25.734
"to contact 10
other potential supporters,"

00:06:25.734 --> 00:06:28.300
saying, "Do it
before the Steelers game,"

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:32.133
despite the fact that there was
no Steelers game on Sunday.

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:33.400
[ Laughter ]
The team had a bye week

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.834
and any Pittsburgher worth their
salt would tell you

00:06:35.834 --> 00:06:38.267
that not knowing the Steelers
had a bye week

00:06:38.267 --> 00:06:40.334
[ Changes accent ]
is a total jagoff move.

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:41.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:42.334
But I'm being hard on him.

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:43.801
I do think Oz knows
Pittsburgh well,

00:06:43.801 --> 00:06:46.734
based on this clip he put out,
where he, very naturally,

00:06:46.734 --> 00:06:48.434
mentioned what the city
is known for.

00:06:48.434 --> 00:06:50.968
-I love,
love being in Pittsburgh.

00:06:50.968 --> 00:06:52.501
Now, people think I come here
for the food,

00:06:52.501 --> 00:06:54.834
and I do like beer
and sandwiches,

00:06:54.834 --> 00:06:56.300
but it's the food
for thought

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.868
that I really came
to Pittsburgh for.

00:06:57.868 --> 00:07:00.400
-Okay, Russian
spy from the '50s.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:01.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.467 --> 00:07:02.901
[ Slavic accent ]
Hello, local barkeep.

00:07:02.901 --> 00:07:05.534
I'm here for a beer,
and sandwiches.

00:07:05.534 --> 00:07:07.434
[ Laughter and applause ]
Also, is true there is

00:07:07.434 --> 00:07:09.534
nuke-ular power plant in town?

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:11.567
[ Laughter ]
How would curious visitor

00:07:11.567 --> 00:07:13.033
take tour to see up close?

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:14.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:17.100
Part of the reason Fetterman's
win was such a big deal was

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.367
because many
in the Republican bubble

00:07:19.367 --> 00:07:20.734
clearly thought
it was impossible.

00:07:20.734 --> 00:07:23.033
Some right-wing pundits
straight-up said, in advance,

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:25.567
there was no way it could happen
and that it would be ridiculous

00:07:25.567 --> 00:07:27.834
to wake up on Wednesday
to a Fetterman victory.

00:07:27.834 --> 00:07:29.334
-It's not about the person.

00:07:29.334 --> 00:07:30.501
It's about the party.

00:07:30.501 --> 00:07:31.767
It's not about the individual.

00:07:31.767 --> 00:07:32.801
It's about the group.

00:07:33.701 --> 00:07:35.133
And, to prove it,
they can even run

00:07:35.133 --> 00:07:37.767
mentally defective candidates
who can barely speak

00:07:37.767 --> 00:07:40.133
and not only expect them
to [ Raising voice ] "win,"

00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:42.167
but expect you to accept
the outcome,

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:44.467
no matter how transparently
absurd it is.

00:07:45.801 --> 00:07:47.133
On November 9th,
they'll be telling you

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:49.801
that John Fetterman got
81 million votes in Pennsylvania

00:07:49.801 --> 00:07:51.000
and they'll threaten
to put you in jail,

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.100
if you don't believe it.

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:53.267
Why wouldn't they do that?

00:07:53.267 --> 00:07:54.767
It worked with Joe Biden.

00:07:54.767 --> 00:07:56.067
-[ As Carlson ]
Why wouldn't they do that?

00:07:56.067 --> 00:07:57.601
Why wouldn't they tell you
John Fetterman won

00:07:57.601 --> 00:07:59.801
and threaten to put you in jail,
if you don't believe it?

00:07:59.801 --> 00:08:01.400
When you're in jail,
why wouldn't they put you

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:02.868
on laundry duty?
And, when you tell them

00:08:02.868 --> 00:08:04.300
you've never done
your own laundry before

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:05.801
and don't know how it works,

00:08:05.801 --> 00:08:07.434
why wouldn't the other inmates
laugh at you?

00:08:07.434 --> 00:08:08.801
And when you tell them
to stop laughing,

00:08:08.801 --> 00:08:10.534
because it's not funny,
why wouldn't they put you

00:08:10.534 --> 00:08:12.534
[ Laughter ]
in the dryer, where you would
get tossed around --

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:15.701
with a load of their underpants,
I should add -- for 45 minutes?

00:08:15.701 --> 00:08:17.267
Why wouldn't they do that?

00:08:17.267 --> 00:08:18.300
[ Laughter ]
Because they did it to me.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:19.901
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.901 --> 00:08:21.133
In high school.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:22.000
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.167
And again in college.

00:08:23.167 --> 00:08:24.400
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.834
I bet, when Tucker
woke up this morning

00:08:25.834 --> 00:08:27.334
and saw the results,
he made that face

00:08:27.334 --> 00:08:29.434
he always makes,
like he buzzed in on "Jeopardy!"

00:08:29.434 --> 00:08:30.868
and forgot what
he was going to say.

00:08:30.868 --> 00:08:32.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:32.033 --> 00:08:33.868
And yet, Fetterman
very much did win,

00:08:33.868 --> 00:08:36.133
as Tucker's own network
explained this morning.

00:08:36.133 --> 00:08:38.834
-When it comes to the state
of Pennsylvania,

00:08:38.834 --> 00:08:41.234
why did Dr. Oz lose?

00:08:41.234 --> 00:08:44.634
Well, it looks like,
according to the exit polling,

00:08:44.634 --> 00:08:46.467
it's because Fetterman won!

00:08:46.467 --> 00:08:47.300
-Yeah!

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:48.667 --> 00:08:51.067
[ Cheering ]
That is,

00:08:51.067 --> 00:08:52.767
historically, how it works.

00:08:52.767 --> 00:08:53.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.868 --> 00:08:55.701
When one candidate loses,
the other wins.

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.868
Although, in fairness,
there are probably Republicans

00:08:57.868 --> 00:08:59.067
who need that explained to them.

00:08:59.067 --> 00:09:02.234
[ As Walker ]
Whoa! If Warnock loses, I win?

00:09:02.234 --> 00:09:05.601
Ohhhhh, that is not a good idea.

00:09:05.601 --> 00:09:08.234
Now, again, there are many races
that have yet to be called

00:09:08.234 --> 00:09:10.567
and, still, a wide range
of possibility.

00:09:10.567 --> 00:09:12.534
Current projections,
as of this taping,

00:09:12.534 --> 00:09:13.701
range anywhere from Democrats

00:09:13.701 --> 00:09:14.901
holding both the House
and Senate

00:09:14.901 --> 00:09:16.968
to razor-thin majorities
for Republicans.

00:09:16.968 --> 00:09:19.567
But, from what we already know,
this election went much better

00:09:19.567 --> 00:09:21.534
than Joe Biden could've
possibly expected,

00:09:21.534 --> 00:09:24.000
given the stiff political
head winds he was facing

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.801
and history,
because incumbent parties

00:09:25.801 --> 00:09:28.601
almost always lose tons
of seats in the midterms.

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:30.200
And, yet, Biden managed
to outperform

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:33.701
those expectations, despite
constant second-guessing,

00:09:33.701 --> 00:09:35.901
even from his fellow
Democrats, about his strategy.

00:09:35.901 --> 00:09:38.501
-It's a better night than
expected for the Democrats.

00:09:38.501 --> 00:09:40.534
You know, what are you hearing
from the White House?

00:09:40.534 --> 00:09:42.467
-A big change of mood
from the White House

00:09:42.467 --> 00:09:43.801
in the past 24 hours.

00:09:43.801 --> 00:09:47.501
They feel excitement,
mixed with some validation,

00:09:47.501 --> 00:09:49.300
because they managed,
they think,

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:50.734
to buck a historic trend --

00:09:50.734 --> 00:09:52.601
they didn't lose dozens
of seats,

00:09:52.601 --> 00:09:54.133
the way previous
presidents have.

00:09:54.133 --> 00:09:57.934
-So, the lesson is
don't bet against Joe Biden.

00:09:57.934 --> 00:09:59.701
-Don't bet against Biden.
-Politically,

00:09:59.701 --> 00:10:01.834
the guy always finds a way,
it seems.

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.367
-That's right --
whatever you think of him,

00:10:03.367 --> 00:10:05.300
never bet against an old man

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.334
who's spent more time
in Scranton dive bars

00:10:07.334 --> 00:10:09.100
than most people have
at their actual jobs.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:10.734
[ Laughter ]
Joe Biden is

00:10:10.734 --> 00:10:12.801
the Mike Ehrmantraut
of American politics.

00:10:12.801 --> 00:10:15.434
[ Laughter ]
You think you can jump him
on a dark street

00:10:15.434 --> 00:10:17.267
and take his wallet
and, the next thing you know,

00:10:17.267 --> 00:10:18.434
you're rolling on the ground,
yelling,

00:10:18.434 --> 00:10:20.434
"My arm! You broke my arm!"
[ Laughter ]

00:10:20.434 --> 00:10:22.367
[ As Mike ]
Here's what we're going
to do now.

00:10:22.367 --> 00:10:24.834
[ Laughter ]

00:10:24.834 --> 00:10:26.300
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.734
Finally, finally, found it,
right at the last minute.

00:10:28.734 --> 00:10:30.567
[ Laughter ]
You know, we have a tendency

00:10:30.567 --> 00:10:32.534
to think of Biden
as a doddering old man

00:10:32.534 --> 00:10:34.901
because, you know, he's an old
man who sometimes dotters,

00:10:34.901 --> 00:10:36.434
[ Laughter ]
but after last night's results,

00:10:36.434 --> 00:10:37.767
I'm starting to think
he might actually be

00:10:37.767 --> 00:10:39.601
the greatest political
mastermind of our generation.

00:10:39.601 --> 00:10:41.834
Maybe the whole Mr. Magoo thing
is a put-on.

00:10:41.834 --> 00:10:43.767
You know how he's always putting
his head in his hands

00:10:43.767 --> 00:10:45.033
while answering questions

00:10:45.033 --> 00:10:48.200
or getting stuck onstage
like a motion center Santa Claus

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:49.834
[ Laughter ]
that runs out of batteries.

00:10:49.834 --> 00:10:51.834
Maybe it's all an act
to disguise the fact

00:10:51.834 --> 00:10:53.667
that he's actually
a Machiavellian genius

00:10:53.667 --> 00:10:56.067
who's constantly doing
electoral math in his head.

00:10:56.067 --> 00:10:57.567
While the rest of us
are having fun,

00:10:57.567 --> 00:10:59.634
laughing at his gaffes,
he's sitting there, saying --

00:10:59.634 --> 00:11:01.133
[ As Biden ]
Laugh it up, mother[bleep]!

00:11:01.133 --> 00:11:03.267
[ Laughter ]
I'm about to have
the best midterm result

00:11:03.267 --> 00:11:04.968
for a sitting president
in two decades.

00:11:04.968 --> 00:11:06.934
Biden's performance last night
was certainly

00:11:06.934 --> 00:11:08.267
much better than Donald Trump's,

00:11:08.267 --> 00:11:09.968
who's getting all the blame
from his party

00:11:09.968 --> 00:11:12.167
for backing a bunch of weirdos,
clowns, and bozos

00:11:12.167 --> 00:11:14.200
[ Laughter ]
who got creamed in their races.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:15.868
Last night was, if nothing else,

00:11:15.868 --> 00:11:18.968
clearly a strong repudiation
of Trumpism from voters

00:11:18.968 --> 00:11:20.601
and that's according
to almost everyone,

00:11:20.601 --> 00:11:22.834
except, of course --
brace yourselves --

00:11:22.834 --> 00:11:23.868
Trump himself.

00:11:23.868 --> 00:11:24.801
[ Laughter ]
-You've endorsed more

00:11:24.801 --> 00:11:26.968
than 330 candidates

00:11:26.968 --> 00:11:28.534
this election cycle.

00:11:28.534 --> 00:11:33.133
Tonight, win or lose,
the results for Republicans,

00:11:33.133 --> 00:11:36.367
how much of that will be
because of Donald Trump?

00:11:36.367 --> 00:11:39.234
-Well, I think, if they win,
I should get all the credit;

00:11:39.234 --> 00:11:40.300
[ Laughter ]
and, if they lose,

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.133
I should not be blamed
at all, okay?

00:11:42.133 --> 00:11:45.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:47.501 --> 00:11:48.901
-I don't think
that's how it works,

00:11:48.901 --> 00:11:51.400
although I'm sure it's not
the first time he's tried.

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.467
[ As Trump ]
I want to bet $100 on the Jets,

00:11:53.467 --> 00:11:55.133
but here's the thing --
if they win, you pay me.

00:11:55.133 --> 00:11:57.000
If they lose,
I get my money back.

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.434
[ Laughter ]

00:11:58.434 --> 00:12:00.300
I mean, of course,
that's what Trump would say.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:01.901
That's how he's operated
his whole life.

00:12:01.901 --> 00:12:03.667
He wants credit for everything
and blame for nothing.

00:12:03.667 --> 00:12:05.834
He's the definition
of a "Heads, I win;

00:12:05.834 --> 00:12:07.267
tails, you lose" kind of guy,

00:12:07.267 --> 00:12:10.000
except, he still
somehow manages to lose.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.534
[ As Trump ]
Heads, I win; tails, you lose.

00:12:11.534 --> 00:12:12.801
And now let's flip the coin.

00:12:12.801 --> 00:12:15.601
And it has been snatched
out of the air by the IRS.

00:12:15.601 --> 00:12:16.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:16.667 --> 00:12:18.667
I owe them $1 billion
in back taxes

00:12:18.667 --> 00:12:20.567
and they're taking it
one quarter at a time.

00:12:20.567 --> 00:12:21.734
[ Laughter ]

00:12:21.734 --> 00:12:23.834
So, Democrats won a bunch
of key races last night,

00:12:23.834 --> 00:12:26.400
despite dire predictions
of a red wave that fizzled out.

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:28.701
Now, control of both the House
and the Senate is,

00:12:28.701 --> 00:12:30.534
as of this taping,
still up for grabs,

00:12:30.534 --> 00:12:31.968
which is, in itself,

00:12:31.968 --> 00:12:34.133
a wild outcome
and a huge disaster

00:12:34.133 --> 00:12:35.634
for Republicans,
among many other things.

00:12:35.634 --> 00:12:37.767
We learned last night
that people are just tired

00:12:37.767 --> 00:12:40.033
of Donald Trump's clown car
of bozos and dip[bleep].

00:12:40.033 --> 00:12:42.000
They want to protect democracy.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.567
They want to protect
reproductive rights.

00:12:43.567 --> 00:12:44.934
They want competent governance

00:12:44.934 --> 00:12:47.300
and they want to vote
for candidates in one election

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:49.300
who aren't going to ignore
their votes in the next one.

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:50.801
They just want to go
about their lives

00:12:50.801 --> 00:12:53.234
like ordinary Americans
and enjoy their...

00:12:53.234 --> 00:12:54.734
-Beer and sandwiches.

00:12:54.734 --> 00:12:56.734
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:12:56.734 --> 00:12:58.467
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:58.467 --> 00:13:02.133
♪♪

